## 5. LLM insight summary API (Week 7)

**Purpose:** Natural-language summaries over aggregate tables, with deterministic fallback when the LLM is unavailable (`ARCHITECTURE_DEEP.md`: template fallback; never block aggregate refresh).

**Input — aggregate tables the summarizer may read (read-only):**

| Table |
|-------|
| `skill_demand_weekly` |
| `tool_demand_weekly` |
| `sector_summary_weekly` |
| `geo_demand_weekly` |
| `skill_velocity` |
| `skill_co_occurrence` |

Optional joins to reference data (`skills`, `industry_sectors`, `job_postings`) must stay within the same allowlists as `sql-guardrails.mdc` when SQL is generated.

**Output object (single summary record):**

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `summary_text` | `str` | Human-readable paragraph(s) |
| `is_llm_generated` | `bool` | `true` if produced by the LLM adapter; `false` if template/deterministic |
| `generated_at` | `str` | ISO 8601 UTC |
| `skill_label` | `str \| None` | Set when the summary scope is a single skill; else `null` |
| `sector_label` | `str \| None` | Set when the summary scope is a single sector; else `null` |

Global or multi-dimension summaries may set **both** `skill_label` and `sector_label` to `null`.

**Fallback when LLM unavailable:**

1. Build **`summary_text`** from a **deterministic template** (fixed sentence patterns filled with latest aggregate metrics from the tables above).
2. Set **`is_llm_generated`** to **`false`**.
3. Set **`generated_at`** to the refresh completion time.
4. Do **not** fail or skip the analytics refresh; log at info level without PII (`structlog`).

